{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.93,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["SW6", "R34", "R35"],
      "pins": ["SW6.1", "SW6.2", "SW6.3", "SW6.4", "R34.1", "R34.2", "R35.1", "R35.2"],
      "nets": ["/CAN0_N", "/CAN0_P", "/CAN1_N", "/CAN1_P", "Net-(R34-Pad2)", "Net-(R35-Pad2)"],
      "observed": "The two poles of SW6 connect CAN0_P to CAN1_P through pins 4 and 3, and connect the R34 and R35 ends through pins 1 and 2. R34 and R35 are each 120R, with their other ends on /CAN0_N and /CAN1_N respectively. Thus closing the switches couples the CAN buses instead of placing a termination resistor across each bus’s P and N lines.",
      "expected": "The specification describes two isolated CAN buses. Their differential pairs should remain separate; if SW6 is intended to switch termination, each 120R resistor should be switched across the P and N lines of its respective bus.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/CAN0_P : ... SW6.4(passive) ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/CAN1_P : ... SW6.3(passive) ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/CAN0_N : ... R34.1(1,passive) ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/CAN1_N : ... R35.1(1,passive) ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(R34-Pad2) : R34.2(2,passive) SW6.1(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(R35-Pad2) : R35.2(2,passive) SW6.2(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "With the relevant switch poles closed, the nominally isolated CAN buses become coupled: their positive lines are directly joined, and their negative lines are linked through the two 120R resistors. This can disrupt CAN signaling and termination, and may defeat bus isolation.",
      "confidence": 0.93
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomaly detected: SW6 and its associated 120R resistors couple the two CAN buses rather than providing separate differential-pair termination. This conflicts with the specification’s description of isolated CAN buses."
}

